see textkit version "0.2" from "textkit.lib".

(src/availability.vox: read the grid; answer "is this person free at
 meeting N"; the warnings; write an empty grid.)

a map called 'unavailable at' is {}.
a list called warnings is [].
a text called 'the availability note' is "".

To 'a list of names contains' with a list called items and a text called target.
  For each item in items,
    if item is target then, Return a boolean, true..
  Return a boolean, false.

To 'a fresh unavailable row'.
  a list called row is [].
  For each 'meeting number' from 1 to 'meeting count', append false to row.
  Return a list, row.

To 'the header names from' with a text called 'the header line'.
  a list called cells is 'split on' of 'the header line' and ",".
  a text called 'the first cell' is element 1 of cells.
  a text called 'the meeting label' is "Meeting".
  a number called 'the first data column' is 1.
  If 'the first cell' is 'the meeting label' then, Set 'the first data column' to 2.
  a list called 'the header names' is [].
  For each 'column number' from 'the first data column' to cells's length,
    a text called 'the header cell' is element 'column number' of cells,
    a text called 'the header name' is trim of 'the header cell',
    append 'the header name' to 'the header names'.
  Return a list, 'the header names'.

To 'warn about the header names' with a list called 'the header names'.
  For each 'header name' in 'the header names',
    if {'a list of names contains' of names and 'header name'} is false then,
      append "{'header name'} is in the grid but not in the names file, column ignored" to warnings..
  For each person in names,
    if {'a list of names contains' of 'the header names' and person} is false then,
      append "{person} has no column in the grid, treated as always available" to warnings..

To 'prepare rows for' with a list called 'the header names'.
  For each person in 'the header names',
    a list called 'the fresh row' is 'a fresh unavailable row',
    Set 'unavailable at''s "{person}" to 'the fresh row'.

To 'mark unavailable' with a text called person and a number called 'meeting number'.
  a list called row is 'unavailable at''s "{person}".
  Set element 'meeting number' of row to true.
  Set 'unavailable at''s "{person}" to row.

To 'read a data row' with a text called 'the data line' and a list called 'the header names' and a number called 'meeting number' and a number called 'the first data column'.
  a list called cells is 'split on' of 'the data line' and ",".
  For each 'column number' from 'the first data column' to cells's length,
    a number called 'the header index' is {'column number' subtract 'the first data column'} add 1,
    if 'the header index' is less than or equal to 'the header names''s length then,
      a text called person is element 'the header index' of 'the header names',
      a text called cell is element 'column number' of cells,
      a text called 'the trimmed cell' is trim of cell,
      if 'the trimmed cell' is "1" then, 'mark unavailable' of person and 'meeting number'...

To 'load the grid from' with a text called path.
  If path is not available then,
    Set 'the availability note' to "no grid at {path}, everyone is available",
    Return.
  Set 'the availability note' to "read from {path}".
  Open a file for reading called 'the grid file' at path.
  a buffer called 'the current line'.
  a list called 'the grid lines' is [].
  Read line from 'the grid file' into 'the current line'.
  While 'the current line' is not empty,
    a text called 'the raw line' is 'the current line' as text,
    a text called 'the trimmed line' is trim of 'the raw line',
    if 'the trimmed line' is not empty then, append 'the trimmed line' to 'the grid lines'.
    Read line from 'the grid file' into 'the current line'.
  Close 'the grid file'.
  If 'the grid lines''s length is 0 then, Return.
  a text called 'the first line' is element 1 of 'the grid lines'.
  a buffer called 'the first line as a buffer' is 'the first line'.
  a number called 'the first byte' is byte 1 of 'the first line as a buffer'.
  a list called 'the header names' is [].
  a number called 'the first data row' is 1.
  a number called 'the first data column' is 1.
  If 'the first byte' is greater than or equal to 48 and 'the first byte' is less than or equal to 57 then,
    append "the grid has no header row, columns taken in names-file order" to warnings,
    For each person in names, append person to 'the header names'.
  Otherwise,
    Set 'the header names' to 'the header names from' of 'the first line',
    'warn about the header names' of 'the header names',
    Set 'the first data row' to 2,
    a list called 'the header cells' is 'split on' of 'the first line' and ",",
    a text called 'the first header cell' is element 1 of 'the header cells',
    if 'the first header cell' is "Meeting" then, Set 'the first data column' to 2.
  'prepare rows for' of 'the header names'.
  a number called 'the meeting number' is 1.
  For each 'row number' from 'the first data row' to 'the grid lines''s length,
    if 'the meeting number' is less than or equal to 'meeting count' then,
      a text called 'the data line' is element 'row number' of 'the grid lines',
      'read a data row' of 'the data line' and 'the header names' and 'the meeting number' and 'the first data column'.
    Set 'the meeting number' to {'the meeting number' add 1}.

To 'is free for meeting' with a text called person and a number called 'meeting number'.
  a list called row is 'unavailable at''s "{person}".
  If row's length is 0 then, Return a boolean, true.
  a boolean called 'the person is unavailable' is element 'meeting number' of row.
  Return a boolean, 'the person is unavailable' is false.

To 'write an empty grid to' with a text called path.
  If path is available then,
    Print "scheduler: {path} already exists, not overwriting it",
    Exit 1.
  Open a file for writing called 'the grid file' at path.
  On error print "scheduler: cannot write {path}", exit 1.
  a text called 'the header row' is join of names and ",".
  Write "Meeting,{'the header row'}\n" to 'the grid file'.
  a list called 'the zero cells' is [].
  For each person in names, append "0" to 'the zero cells'.
  a text called 'the zero row' is join of 'the zero cells' and ",".
  For each 'meeting number' from 1 to 'meeting count',
    a text called 'the meeting label' is 'the label of meeting' of 'meeting number',
    Write "{'the meeting label'},{'the zero row'}\n" to 'the grid file'.
  Close 'the grid file'.
  Print "Wrote an empty grid for {'meeting count'} meetings and {names's length} people to {path}".
  Exit 0.
